.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt ASN1_ITEM_D2I_BIO 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ASN1_item_d2i_ex ,
.Nm ASN1_item_d2i ,
.Nm ASN1_item_d2i_bio_ex ,
.Nm ASN1_item_d2i_bio ,
.Nm ASN1_item_d2i_fp_ex ,
.Nm ASN1_item_d2i_fp ,
.Nm ASN1_item_i2d_mem_bio ,
.Nm ASN1_item_pack ,
.Nm ASN1_item_unpack_ex ,
.Nm ASN1_item_unpack
.Nd decode and encode DER-encoded ASN.1 structures
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/asn1.h
.Ft ASN1_VALUE *
.Fo ASN1_item_d2i_ex
.Fa "ASN1_VALUE **pval"
.Fa "const unsigned char **in"
.Fa "long len"
.Fa "const ASN1_ITEM *it"
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *libctx"
.Fa "const char *propq"
.Fc
.Ft ASN1_VALUE *
.Fo ASN1_item_d2i
.Fa "ASN1_VALUE **pval"
.Fa "const unsigned char **in"
.Fa "long len"
.Fa "const ASN1_ITEM *it"
.Fc
.Ft void *
.Fo ASN1_item_d2i_bio_ex
.Fa "const ASN1_ITEM *it"
.Fa "BIO *in"
.Fa "void *x"
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *libctx"
.Fa "const char *propq"
.Fc
.Ft void *
.Fo ASN1_item_d2i_bio
.Fa "const ASN1_ITEM *it"
.Fa "BIO *in"
.Fa "void *x"
.Fc
.Ft void *
.Fo ASN1_item_d2i_fp_ex
.Fa "const ASN1_ITEM *it"
.Fa "FILE *in"
.Fa "void *x"
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *libctx"
.Fa "const char *propq"
.Fc
.Ft void *
.Fo ASN1_item_d2i_fp
.Fa "const ASN1_ITEM *it"
.Fa "FILE *in"
.Fa "void *x"
.Fc
.Ft BIO *
.Fo ASN1_item_i2d_mem_bio
.Fa "const ASN1_ITEM *it"
.Fa "const ASN1_VALUE *val"
.Fc
.Ft ASN1_STRING *
.Fo ASN1_item_pack
.Fa "void *obj"
.Fa "const ASN1_ITEM *it"
.Fa "ASN1_STRING **oct"
.Fc
.Ft void *
.Fo ASN1_item_unpack
.Fa "const ASN1_STRING *oct"
.Fa "const ASN1_ITEM *it"
.Fc
.Ft void *
.Fo ASN1_item_unpack_ex
.Fa "const ASN1_STRING *oct"
.Fa "const ASN1_ITEM *it"
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *libctx"
.Fa "const char *propq"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn ASN1_item_d2i_ex
decodes the contents of the data stored in
.Em *in
of length
.Fa len
which must be a DER-encoded ASN.1 structure, using the ASN.1 template
.Fa it .
It places the result in
.Em *pval
unless
.Fa pval
is NULL. If
.Em *pval
is non-NULL on entry then the
.Vt ASN1_VALUE
present there will be reused.
Otherwise a new
.Vt ASN1_VALUE
will be allocated.
If any algorithm fetches are required during the process then they will
use the
.Vt OSSL_LIB_CTX Ns provided
in the
.Fa libctx
parameter and the property query string in
.Fa propq .
See
.Xr crypto 7
for more information about algorithm fetching.
On exit
.Em *in
will be updated to point to the next byte in the buffer after the
decoded structure.
.Pp
.Fn ASN1_item_d2i
is the same as
.Fn ASN1_item_d2i_ex
except that the default OSSL_LIB_CTX is used (i.e.
NULL) and with a NULL property query string.
.Pp
.Fn ASN1_item_d2i_bio_ex
decodes the contents of its input BIO
.Fa in ,
which must be a DER-encoded ASN.1 structure, using the ASN.1 template
.Fa it
and places the result in
.Em *pval
unless
.Fa pval
is NULL. If
.Fa in
is NULL it returns NULL, else a pointer to the parsed structure.
If any algorithm fetches are required during the process then they will
use the
.Vt OSSL_LIB_CTX
provided in the
.Fa libctx
parameter and the property query string in
.Fa propq .
See
.Xr crypto 7
for more information about algorithm fetching.
.Pp
.Fn ASN1_item_d2i_bio
is the same as
.Fn ASN1_item_d2i_bio_ex
except that the default
.Vt OSSL_LIB_CTX
is used (i.e.
NULL) and with a NULL property query string.
.Pp
.Fn ASN1_item_d2i_fp_ex
is the same as
.Fn ASN1_item_d2i_bio_ex
except that a FILE pointer is provided instead of a BIO.
.Pp
.Fn ASN1_item_d2i_fp
is the same as
.Fn ASN1_item_d2i_fp_ex
except that the default
.Vt OSSL_LIB_CTX
is used (i.e.
NULL) and with a NULL property query string.
.Pp
.Fn ASN1_item_i2d_mem_bio
encodes the given ASN.1 value
.Fa val
using the ASN.1 template
.Fa it
and returns the result in a memory BIO.
.Pp
.Fn ASN1_item_pack
encodes the given ASN.1 value in
.Fa obj
using the ASN.1 template
.Fa it
and returns an
.Vt ASN1_STRING
object.
If the passed in
.Em *oct
is not NULL then this is used to store the returned result, otherwise a
new
.Vt ASN1_STRING
object is created.
If
.Fa oct
is not NULL and
.Em *oct
is NULL then the returned return is also set into
.Em *oct .
If there is an error the optional passed in
.Vt ASN1_STRING
will not be freed, but the previous value may be cleared when
ASN1_STRING_set0(*oct, NULL, 0) is called internally.
.Pp
.Fn ASN1_item_unpack
uses
.Fn ASN1_item_d2i
to decode the DER-encoded
.Vt ASN1_STRING
.Fa oct
using the ASN.1 template
.Fa it .
.Pp
.Fn ASN1_item_unpack_ex
is similar to
.Fn ASN1_item_unpack ,
but uses
.Fn ASN1_item_d2i_ex
so that the
.Fa libctx
and
.Fa propq
can be used when doing algorithm fetching.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn ASN1_item_d2i_bio ,
.Fn ASN1_item_unpack_ex
and
.Fn ASN1_item_unpack
return a pointer to an
.Vt ASN1_VALUE
or NULL on error.
.Pp
.Fn ASN1_item_i2d_mem_bio
returns a pointer to a memory BIO or NULL on error.
.Pp
.Fn ASN1_item_pack
returns a pointer to an
.Vt ASN1_STRING
or NULL on error.
.Sh HISTORY
The functions
.Fn ASN1_item_d2i_ex ,
.Fn ASN1_item_d2i_bio_ex ,
.Fn ASN1_item_d2i_fp_ex
and
.Fn ASN1_item_i2d_mem_bio
were added in OpenSSL 3.0.
.Pp
The function
.Fn ASN1_item_unpack_ex
was added in OpenSSL 3.2.
